CORE
main.cpp
--cpp98
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ condition value used in branch: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ redeclaration after the if: SUCCESS$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
FAILURE
--
N5008 [stmt.pre]/6: the condition declaration's name is scoped to the
substatements; redeclaring it after the if-statement is well-formed.
The name used to leak into the enclosing block ("already declared with
different type").  Header-free.
